{# The .body fragment layout: /base.tpl is swapped for this one when a request asks for a body-only render (render_template.go). The head block is rendered ahead of the body because every template that defines one uses it for custom_css alone, and the timeline preview grid injects a whole fragment with innerHTML -- cards whose CustomSummary/CustomAvatar markup is written against that CSS, on a page that renders no cards itself and so has none of it in its own head. The bulk-operation refresh reads the same fragment but lifts only [data-list-container] out of it, so the style element is neither morphed in nor accumulated there; that path already has the CSS in the page head. A style element is valid in body flow content and goes away with the fragment it arrived in. #}
{% block head %}{% endblock %}{% block body %}{% endblock %}
